{
  "@odata.type": "#microsoft.graph.deviceManagementConfigurationPolicy",
  "description": "Consolidated Device Lock / Device Password policy. Replaces the 6 separate 'Device Password Enabled...' files from the original baseline, which each carried the FULL DeviceLock settings-catalog group (the CSP requires all child settings to travel together under one parent choice setting) but only one of the six had its intended value set correctly — the other five reset the same shared settings back to schema defaults. Deploying more than one of the six to the same device makes Intune flag a genuine settings conflict, and only one value reliably applies. This single policy carries all seven correct CIS L1 values together:\n  - Device Password Enabled: Enabled\n  - Minimum Password Length: 14\n  - Alphanumeric Password Required: Password or Alphanumeric PIN required (strict)\n  - Max Password Failed Attempts: 5\n  - Max Inactivity Time (Device Lock): 15 minutes\n  - Password History: 24\n  - Password Expiration: 0 (not required — current NIST/CIS guidance)",
  "name": "Baseline - Device Password Policy (Consolidated)",
